    "history": {
      "value": "Insight Partners was founded in New York in 1995 by Jeff Horing and Jerry Murdock to back growing software and internet companies. It became known for bets on Twitter, Shopify, Alibaba, Wiz and monday.com, and it now manages about $92 billion after closing a $20 billion fund in 2022. The track record on this page covers its minority stakes only; the companies it bought outright are left out.",
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Insight_Partners",
      "basis": "Founding (1995, New York, Jeff Horing and Jerry Murdock): Wikipedia and the firm's releases ('Founded in 1995'). Bets: Twitter's $100M round of 2009, Shopify's 2013 Series C, Alibaba before its listing, Wiz's 2020 Series A (bought by Google in 2026), monday.com's 2017 Series B, all on the firm's own portfolio pages. Assets: $92,178,934,483 regulatory assets under management on the adviser's Form ADV of 2026-09-09 (CRD 142994, Item 5.F), about $90B in the press; Fund XII 'with total capital commitments in excess of $20 billion' (the firm's counsel, 2022-02-24). The latest close is $12.5B across Fund XIII, the Fund XIII Growth Buyout Fund and Opportunities Fund II (January 2025). BOUNDARY (PRO-165): the firm makes both minority growth investments and buyouts from the same fund family; the record on the page covers minority positions only, and every transaction in which the firm alone or with co-investors took at least half the voting equity is excluded as a control position (the count and the largest exclusions are in report.md). Nothing true dropped: the fund ladder, the buyout annex and growth buyout vehicles, the continuation funds of 2019, 2022 and 2024 and the London and Tel Aviv offices live in the funds and aum bases."
    },
