      "basis": "Sizes from the firm's own releases and its counsel's notes; the vehicles' Form Ds file 'Indefinite' offerings with partial sold amounts, so every size rests on the release and no entry carries an accession (COLLECTION.md §11). XIII and related funds $12.5B: Fund XIII, the Fund XIII Growth Buyout Fund and Opportunities Fund II closed together (https://www.willkie.com/news/2025/01/willkie-represents-insight-partners-in-combined-12-5-billion-closing). XII 'in excess of $20 billion' with its co-investment fund (https://www.willkie.com/news/2022/02/insight-partners-closes-20-billion-fundraise). Opportunities Fund I $1.56B (https://www.insightpartners.com/ideas/insight-partners-closes-1-56b-opportunities-fund-to-support-market-leading-software-companies/). XI $9.5B (https://www.insightpartners.com/ideas/insight-partners-closes-growth-equity-technology-fund-xi-at-9-5-billion/). X $6.3B (https://www.insightpartners.com/ideas/software-investor-insight-venture-partners-closes-6-3-billion-fund-x/). IX $3.29B and the Growth-Buyout Coinvestment Fund $1.46B, 'a co-investment vehicle that will co-invest in control transactions with Fund IX' (https://www.insightpartners.com/ideas/insight-venture-partners-closes-growth-equity-funds-totaling-4-75-billion-2/). Coinvestment Fund III $510M (https://www.insightpartners.com/ideas/insight-venture-partners-closes-new-co-investment-fund-totaling-510-million-to-invest-alongside-insight-venture-partners-viii/). VIII $2.57B (https://www.insightpartners.com/ideas/insight-venture-partners-closes-new-fund-totaling-2-57-billion/). VII about $1.5B of institutional and $70M of affiliate commitments, and Coinvestment Fund II $450M (https://www.insightpartners.com/ideas/insight-venture-partners-closes-new-funds-totaling-2-billion/). Not listed: Funds I to VI (1995 to 2007; no release on the site), the XII Buyout Annex Fund (inside the $20B), Opportunities Fund II (inside the $12.5B), the continuation funds of 2019, 2022 and 2024 ($1.5B, https://www.willkie.com/news/2024/10/willkie-advises-insight-partners-on-formation-of-1-5-billion-continuation-fund-iii), Insight Vision Capital II and the Seed Managers Fund."
